/E (She picked up the old photograph of Elara and looked at it again. Her mother's smile seemed different now. Not happier. Not sadder. Just different. Luna wondered how many things about her childhood she had forgotten. She closed her eyes and tried to remember the night Elara disappeared. She could see the room. She could see the rain outside. She could see her mother's dark hair. She could see the black book in her hands. But then there was a blank space. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
