/T (When Luna was ten, she had once lost a small silver music box that her grandmother had given her. She had searched everywhere for it but never found it. It was not something she thought about often. If the book changed that memory, perhaps the result would be small enough to understand. Luna opened the black book and wrote carefully: I wish I had never lost the silver music box. The words stayed on the page for a few seconds. Then they slowly faded. The book closed by itself. Luna waited. Nothing happened. She almost felt relieved. Maybe the book had stopped working. Maybe she had finally reached its limit.)
