/E (Luna slowly stood up. She wanted to believe that what she had just seen was only a dream, but the wetness on her cheeks told her otherwise. She had been crying. She touched her face and looked at her fingers. Then she noticed something on her palm. A tiny white flower petal was lying there. Luna stared at it. She had seen those flowers in the garden. She had held nothing in her hand before entering that strange place. There was no way a flower petal from a dream could be sitting on her palm.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [3]
