/T (He opened the box. Inside were several photographs, a silver key, and a folded piece of paper. Luna picked up the first photograph. It showed two little girls sitting beneath the garden tree. Luna recognized herself. Beside her was Mira. They were both smiling. Luna touched Mira's face. A strange warmth moved through her. For a moment, she could almost hear the little girl's voice. Luna, wait for me. She quickly placed the photograph down. Then she opened the folded paper. It contained only one sentence in Elara's handwriting: If Luna remembers Mira, the book has already found her.)
