/T (The letters were uneven because she had been very young. At the top of the page was a drawing of two girls standing under a large tree. Beneath them was a sentence written in bright pencil. Mira and Luna will always find each other. Luna stared at it. She did not remember writing it. Yet the words felt true. She turned the paper over. On the back was another drawing. This time, there was a black book between the two girls. A small red line had been drawn around it, as if young Luna had been warning someone not to touch it. Under the drawing were three simple words: Don't open it.)
