/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 736 0 R
/E (Luna stood in front of the small wooden door, the silver key resting between her fingers. She could hear her father's breathing behind her, but she did not turn around. The First Writer was standing several steps away, watching her quietly. He had told her that Mira was somewhere beyond this door, somewhere unfinished stories went when their writers could no longer return to them. Luna wanted to open it. She wanted to find her sister. She wanted answers about Elara. But something inside her told her that the door was not simply a way to find Mira. It was a choice. She slowly placed the silver key into the lock. The moment she turned it, the entire library disappeared.)
/Pg 88 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1402 0 obj
<<
