/T (She had never known how much she wanted an ordinary family until she finally had one. Nobody disappeared. Nobody was hiding anything. Nobody was afraid. When dinner ended, Luna helped Mira wash the dishes. Mira splashed a little water toward her, and Luna laughed. It felt so natural that Luna almost forgot that Mira had once been a missing memory. Later, the two sisters sat on the floor of their old bedroom and looked through photographs. There were pictures of birthdays, holidays, school events, and ordinary afternoons. Luna smiled at every one of them.)
