/P 744 0 R
/T (The next morning, Luna decided to test it. She moved the flower vase from the table and placed it near the window. Her mother walked into the room and looked at it. She didn't react. Luna waited. At lunchtime, the vase was back on the table. She moved a chair into another room. A few hours later, it was back where it had always been. She took a family photograph from the wall and placed it inside a drawer. When she returned later, the photograph was hanging on the wall again. Luna stared at it. Nobody had moved those things. The world itself had corrected them. It was as if reality was quietly saying, No. This is how the story goes.)
/E (The next morning, Luna decided to test it. She moved the flower vase from the table and placed it near the window. Her mother walked into the room and looked at it. She didn't react. Luna waited. At lunchtime, the vase was back on the table. She moved a chair into another room. A few hours later, it was back where it had always been. She took a family photograph from the wall and placed it inside a drawer. When she returned later, the photograph was hanging on the wall again. Luna stared at it. Nobody had moved those things. The world itself had corrected them. It was as if reality was quietly saying, No. This is how the story goes.)
