/T (He didn't answer. Luna slowly understood. The First Writer wasn't afraid of what she would write. He was afraid that she would refuse to write at all. Because if she refused, he couldn't control what came next. Luna picked up the pen again. The First Writer watched closely. She opened the book. The final page was blank. She held the pen above it. For a moment, she thought about writing Mira. Then Elara. Then home. Then happiness. But she stopped herself.)
