/Title (The same pen that had changed so many lives was lying beside the book. Luna picked it up slowly. It felt strangely ordinary in her hand. She remembered the first time she had held it. Back then, she had believed the pen was a way to fix everything. If something hurt, she could rewrite it. If someone left, she could bring them back. If she didn't like a memory, she could replace it. But now she understood the danger of that power. A life could not be made perfect simply by removing every painful part of it. Pain was not the only thing that made a life real. Mistakes, choices, losses, happiness, surprises, and even uncertainty belonged to a person's story too.)
