/Title (There were no bills, no broken toys, no dirty dishes left in the sink, no arguments, no tired faces. Nothing ever needed to be repaired because nothing ever truly changed. Luna walked into the kitchen and opened the refrigerator. The same food was inside that she had seen the previous day. She opened a cupboard. The same number of plates. The same cups. Even the flower vase on the table had the same three flowers, in exactly the same position. Luna stepped backward. She suddenly understood that this world did not have a future. It only had a perfect present.)
